**Task**: Survey non-branch-modified jadx files for refactoring opportunities (xmlgen + utils).

---

**1 — `ManifestAttributes.java:191` — Per-call sort of FLAG entries (efficiency, hot path)**

```java
List<Long> attrKeys = new ArrayList<>(attrValuesMap.keySet());
attrKeys.sort((a, b) -> Long.compare(b, a)); // line 192
for (Long key : attrKeys) {
    String attrValue = attrValuesMap.get(key); // re-lookup each value
```

`decode()` is called for every attribute value decoded from the resource table. For FLAG attrs it creates a new `ArrayList`, sorts it, then re-looks up each value via `attrValuesMap.get(key)`. The sort is redundant — `attrValuesMap` doesn't change after `parseValues()` finishes building it. Fix: store a pre-sorted `List<Map.Entry<Long,String>>` in `MAttr` at the end of `parseValues()`, iterate over it directly in `decode()` without any per-call allocation.

---

**2 — `ValuesParser.java:107-133` — Duplicated TYPE_REFERENCE / TYPE_ATTRIBUTE block (simplification/reuse)**

```java
case TYPE_DYNAMIC_REFERENCE:
case TYPE_REFERENCE: {
    String ri = resMap.get(data);
    if (ri == null) {
        String androidRi = AndroidResourcesMap.getResName(data);
        if (androidRi != null) { return "@android:" + androidRi; }
        if (data == 0) { return "0"; }
        return "?unknown_ref: " + Integer.toHexString(data);
    }
    return '@' + ri;
}
case TYPE_ATTRIBUTE: {
    String ri = resMap.get(data);
    if (ri == null) {
        String androidRi = AndroidResourcesMap.getResName(data);
        if (androidRi != null) { return "?android:" + androidRi; }
        return "?unknown_attr_ref: " + Integer.toHexString(data);
    }
    return '?' + ri;
}
```

10-line block duplicated with only the prefix char and fallback string different. Extract:

```java
private String resolveResRef(int data, char prefix) {
    String ri = resMap.get(data);
    if (ri != null) return prefix + ri;
    String androidRi = AndroidResourcesMap.getResName(data);
    if (androidRi != null) return prefix + "android:" + androidRi;
    return prefix + "unknown_ref: " + Integer.toHexString(data);
}
```

(`TYPE_REFERENCE` has a unique `data == 0 → "0"` case that can stay inline or be a parameter.)

---

**3 — `Utils.java:346` vs `ListUtils.java:72` — Identical `map` / `collectionMap` (reuse)**

`Utils.collectionMap(Collection<T>, Function<T,R>)` and `ListUtils.map(Collection<T>, Function<T,R>)` are **byte-for-byte identical** — same null/empty guard, same `ArrayList` construction, same loop. Fix: have `Utils.collectionMap` delegate to `ListUtils.map` (or vice versa, depending on which is the canonical location).

---

**4 — `Utils.java:557` vs `ListUtils.java:94` — Duplicate `last(List)` (reuse)**

`Utils.last(List<T>)` and `ListUtils.last(List<T>)` differ only in that `ListUtils` also handles `null` input. Fix: `Utils.last` delegates to `ListUtils.last`, or the implementations are merged.

---

**5 — `ManifestAttributes.java:178` — `split(":", 2)[1]` allocates an array for a single char split (simplification)**

```java
attrName = attrName.split(":", 2)[1];
```

Allocates a `String[]` just to grab index 1. Replace with:

```java
attrName = attrName.substring(attrName.indexOf(':') + 1);
```

---

**6 — `Utils.java:102` — `String.format` for trivial array suffix (efficiency)**

```java
javaName = String.format("%s[]", smaliNameToJavaName(descString.substring(1, descString.length())));
```

`String.format` carries a regex-parse overhead vs simple concatenation. Replace with:

```java
javaName = smaliNameToJavaName(descString.substring(1)) + "[]";
```

(`substring(1, length())` is also redundant — `substring(1)` is identical.)

---

**7 — `Utils.java:111` — `cleanObjectNameWithInnerClass` is a single-use method with a self-doubting comment (simplification)**

```java
private static String cleanObjectNameWithInnerClass(String obj) {
    // Probably can just update the Utils.cleanObjectName method?
    String result = Utils.cleanObjectName(obj);
    return result.replace('$', '.');
}
```

Called from exactly one site (line 99). The TODO comment itself acknowledges it may be unnecessary abstraction. Inline the one-liner at the call site and delete the method.

---

**8 — `ManifestAttributes.java:220` — `getTypeName().equals("attr")` string comparison in a hot resource loop (efficiency)**

```java
if (ri.getTypeName().equals("attr") && ri.getNamedValues().size() > 1) {
```

`updateAttributes()` is called over the full `resStorage.getResources()` collection, which covers every resource in the APK. A string equality check on every entry is wasteful if `ResourceEntry` has (or could have) an enum type field. Check whether `getTypeName()` can be replaced with a type-code integer comparison; if the type is already represented as an int elsewhere in the parser, comparing ints is significantly cheaper than `String.equals`.

